te for Science & Health Leadership Institute Student Fellows Priestly Discernment Program All Institutes & Centers Resources Registrar Academic Catalog Academic Advising & Support Academic Calendar St. John Paul II Library Study Abroad in Austria Austria Program Home Summer Experience Information for Parents Connect Admission General Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Visit Franciscan Online Programs Transfer Secure Your Enrollment New Student Orientation Austria Study Abroad St. John Paul II Library Tuition & Financial Aid Costs & Fees Tuition & Financial Aid Scholarship International Students Undergraduate Graduate Connect Living Your Faith Chapel Schedule & Info Places to Pray The Franciscans, TOR Housing & Dining Residence Life Households Off-Campus Housing Dining Student Opportunities Student Clubs Outreach Student Employment Baron Athletics Student Resources Student Handbook Wellness Center Connect Alumni & Giving Alumni News & Events Step in Faith Annual Fund Legacy Giving Ways to Give Why FUS? FUS at a Glance Mission, Vision, & Charism Our History Strategic Planning Resources Campus Safety Travel and Accommodations News & Events University News Upcoming Events Franciscan Magazine Open Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Psychology at Franciscan University of Steubenville The Psychology Department at Franciscan University of Steubenville invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, tenure-track position beginning Fall 2027. We seek dedicated educators and dynamic scholars who are passionate about academic excellence and integrating the Catholic faith with psychology . Teaching Load: Four courses per semester (fall and spring), primarily in face-to-face formats. Optional Summer Teaching: Available for those interested in additional opportunities. Why Franciscan? Franciscan University of Steubenville is a passionately Catholic institution in the Franciscan tradition , devoted to academic rigor and transformational education . Located in Steubenville, Ohio, just 24 miles west of the Pittsburgh Airport, our faculty form a mission-driven community committed to faith, scholarship, and mentorship. Who We’re Looking For: We are particularly interested in candidates who: Demonstrate excellence in teaching and mentorship of undergraduate students. Maintain an active research program and integrate undergraduate students into meaningful research experiences. Specialization in clinical or counseling psychology, or a related field. Teaching Opportunities: Course needs include options selected from among the following that best match the candidate’s strengths: Clinical: Intro to Counseling, Intro to Group Counseling, Interview & Assessment, Abnormal Psychology, Personality Theory Faith & Psychology: Human & Spiritual Integration, Spirituality in the Helping Profession, Marriage Family & Spiritual Issues in Counseling Qualifications Ph.D. (or equivalent) in psychology or a related discipline by the time of appointment. ABD candidates will be considered. Commitment to teaching, scholarship, and service in alignment with the mission of Franciscan University . Legally authorized to work in the United States. Visa sponsorship is limited to TN status (Canadian and Mexican citizens only). How to Apply Applicants should submit the following materials electronically to Dr. Joanne Storm Gallagher, Chair, Search Committee, via [email protected] Cover letter outlining interest and qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Former teaching evaluations. Statement of teaching philosophy. Personal statement on alignment with the mission of Franciscan University . Contact information for three professional references. Letters of recommendation will be requested for finalists. Copies of academic transcripts. Official transcripts required upon hire. Application Review Begins: October 1, 2026 (Open until filled). Questions? Contact Dr. Joanne Storm Gallagher at [email protected] . Join us in shaping the next generation of psychologists at Franciscan University! About Franciscan Franciscan University of Steubenville is no ordinary university, and a Franciscan education is no ordinary education. Rather, it’s an education as rigorous and demanding as it is faithful—an education that challenges you intellectually, forms you professionally, and feeds you spiritually. Apply Inquire Visit Give Our Schools All Programs School of Humanities and Social Sciences School of Natural and Applied Sciences School of Online Programming School of Professional Programs School of Theology and Philosophy Franciscan Community Student Life Household Life Residence Life Student Clubs Athletics Alumni & Friends Steubenville Conferences Resources Career Opportunities The Port Visit, Amenities, & Directions Campus Store Campus Safety Title IX Resources Hazing Prevention Student Handbook Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Transfer International Scholarships Tuition & Financial Aid © Franciscan University of Steubenville Contact Us Privacy Policy Directions Nondiscrimination Statement Consumer Information Terms and Conditions Go to Top Apply Request Info Visit Programs Give"
    },
