d experience Mathematics Adjunct teaching load will typically include Calculus I and/or other introductory mathematics courses To apply , applicants should submit the following materials: a cover letter outlining the interest and candidate’s strengths in support of the advertised position, and addressing the mission of Franciscan University of Steubenville current resume or CV unofficial transcripts evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available) The application package must be submitted via email to Dr. Valerie Plaus , Chair, Department of Mathematics & Physical Sciences, at [email protected] . Adjunct Professor of Chemistry POSITION SUMMARY The Department of Mathematics & Physical Sciences at Franciscan University of Steubenville invites applications for multiple positions as Adjunct Instructor beginning Fall 2024.  These are contracted part-time and term-specific faculty position, renewable as needed by the university. Franciscan University of Steubenville is an academically excellent and passionately Catholic university in the Franciscan tradition, located 24 miles west of Pittsburgh International Airport, in Steubenville, Ohio. Qualifications : A Master’s degree in Chemistry, or a related field, or a minimum of BS/BA with 5 years of related experience Chemistry Adjunct teaching load will typically include General/Introductory Chemistry laboratory To apply , applicants should submit the following materials: a cover letter outlining the interest and candidate’s strengths in support of the advertised position, and addressing the mission of Franciscan University of Steubenville current resume or CV unofficial transcripts evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available) The application package must be submitted via email to Dr. Valerie Plaus, Chair, Department of Mathematics & Physical Sciences, at [email protected] . About Franciscan Franciscan University of Steubenville is no ordinary university, and a Franciscan education is no ordinary education. Rather, it’s